            {
                "entry_id": "445cc263-971f-3b87-b65f-a67ccb6f6f84",
                "word": "polaroid",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5ee2bd2d-ad88-40e0-b95c-ecd4379d3b7a",
                        "entry_id": "445cc263-971f-3b87-b65f-a67ccb6f6f84",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "polaroids"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a15a30e3-ab20-3762-ad5f-576a1872e542",
                        "entry_id": "445cc263-971f-3b87-b65f-a67ccb6f6f84",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A sheet of plastic embedded with microscopic crystals of herapathite or similarly acting material, so that light passing through it is polarized."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f23b6e65-2f67-4f39-8a83-31cefff98273",
                                "sense_id": "a15a30e3-ab20-3762-ad5f-576a1872e542",
                                "text": "In the simplest form of this system, applicable to many microscopes, the substage polar consists only of semicircles of polaroid orientated to give respective planes of polarisation at right angles. Polaroids over the eyepieces are orientated so extinguish the inner halves of the exit pupils."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca21e154-e391-42a2-87a2-d8d784fc126c",
                                "sense_id": "a15a30e3-ab20-3762-ad5f-576a1872e542",
                                "text": "If there is no sample in the cell, and the second polaroid is rotated until it is at right angles to the first, the observer will see no light."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "869a1256-e7cc-42eb-8ccd-a98bbca88794",
                                "sense_id": "a15a30e3-ab20-3762-ad5f-576a1872e542",
                                "text": "Polaroids are used as window screens to regulate the amount of light entering the room."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "617ccdfd-3ff5-32a9-b60b-5fb9fdad900f",
                        "entry_id": "445cc263-971f-3b87-b65f-a67ccb6f6f84",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Spectacles made with lenses of this material, once used to view certain 3-D movies, now used as sunglasses."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "in-plural"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4da6f8a2-c1f4-472f-a5c4-3417e56e8121",
                                "sense_id": "617ccdfd-3ff5-32a9-b60b-5fb9fdad900f",
                                "text": "She went to see BWANA DEVIL and, after donning the polaroids, saw correctly."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1041a44-5938-4a00-9bc5-b55eec4b7a74",
                                "sense_id": "617ccdfd-3ff5-32a9-b60b-5fb9fdad900f",
                                "text": "[…]I discovered my old woggle in a cardboard box, together with my Herald Learn-To-Swim certificate (25 yards without touching the bottom), a copy of the Eltham High School magazine and a pair of polaroids I pinched from a 3-D screening of Bwana Devil in 1953."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e576e9b-deff-4ed2-8b0b-56a59563f03b",
                                "sense_id": "617ccdfd-3ff5-32a9-b60b-5fb9fdad900f",
                                "text": "One reel, loaded with a floating or intermediate line, a few braided leaders of varying sinking-rates, a few spare spools of leader-material in 6, 8 and 10lb breaking-strain, a box of assorted fly-patterns, a good pair of polaroids to stop the glare and to protect eyes, and a collapsible line-tray as the rocks are very sharp and soon ruin lines."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "70e93dff-610b-42f5-a8ad-9cf4b7a2b968",
                                "sense_id": "617ccdfd-3ff5-32a9-b60b-5fb9fdad900f",
                                "text": "For while the boy continued to sport his pair of Polaroids, evidently the brilliant afternoon had broken into a drizzle: his damp cargo pants and t-shirt clung to his thin but well-muscled torso while his olive-skinned arms and face appeared as if sugar glazed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d996c66e-7025-481b-8e74-a14ccfbed975",
                                "sense_id": "617ccdfd-3ff5-32a9-b60b-5fb9fdad900f",
                                "text": "I could carry a spare pair of polaroids; however, Steve usually carries an extra pair which should be sufficient back-up for both of us."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "96df44f6-1e24-3188-9050-383b3a441968",
                        "entry_id": "445cc263-971f-3b87-b65f-a67ccb6f6f84",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A camera that develops its own film."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d0739b6f-3ecc-3694-ab12-f7737fa83556",
                        "entry_id": "445cc263-971f-3b87-b65f-a67ccb6f6f84",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A print from such a camera."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8742a59c-8f9c-4ece-aee4-d41425d70f2e",
                                "sense_id": "d0739b6f-3ecc-3694-ab12-f7737fa83556",
                                "text": "Simons slides a pair of Polaroids across the table. They depict a couple of color-lit high schoolers standing in what appears to be an empty warehouse."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "44850ca8-bd47-4a23-a540-c4f3f49ee0ef",
                        "source_entry_id": "445cc263-971f-3b87-b65f-a67ccb6f6f84",
                        "source_sense_description": "print from such a camera",
                        "target_lang_word": "polaroïd",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "polaroïd",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1854c77b-cce1-3cfb-83c7-f6816e186dc5",
                                        "entry_id": "97aa65cd-7bba-3bc0-a1d6-c70ff5293698",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Feuille transparente de résine synthétique qui polarise la lumière."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09dd4c20-a463-4726-90c3-cbfbc0d7d30c",
                                                "sense_id": "1854c77b-cce1-3cfb-83c7-f6816e186dc5",
                                                "text": "L’automobiliste au volant d’une voiture dont le pare-brise est lui aussi en « polaroïd » ne peut être aveuglé par les rayons directs, qui sont interceptés par le verre spécial de ce pare-brise."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f9944182-c967-3640-8914-7594187b1dea",
                                        "entry_id": "97aa65cd-7bba-3bc0-a1d6-c70ff5293698",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "(en français 1951) Appareil photographique instantané permettant d’obtenir directement des photographies argentiques, sans passer par des opérations séparées de développement du film et de tirage sur papier."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50e82831-c3ff-437d-9a6e-99d0c1bca6d2",
                                                "sense_id": "f9944182-c967-3640-8914-7594187b1dea",
                                                "text": "Je n'ai rien, rien !... Il n’y a pas de négatifs quand on travaille au polaroïd…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "385ff4d3-c0cf-4a08-9216-b7abe08697dc",
                                                "sense_id": "f9944182-c967-3640-8914-7594187b1dea",
                                                "text": "Le polaroïd de l’époque faisait de meilleures photos que mon premier APN Fotoman Logitech en 356 niveaux de gris gros comme un radio téléphone et connectable sur port RS232 pour enfin voir sur le PC la trentaine de photos."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f4e6e0b-ffb2-467e-94ce-d185c3be30e5",
                                                "sense_id": "f9944182-c967-3640-8914-7594187b1dea",
                                                "text": "Basquiat lui demande de prendre un cliché d’eux, avec son Polaroïd."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b8f4fba-d4cc-3c1b-bf33-86afd2a1ad8c",
                                        "entry_id": "97aa65cd-7bba-3bc0-a1d6-c70ff5293698",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Photographie obtenue avec cet appareil."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "543079cb-4c4c-44b4-b28d-a99c514315ce",
                                                "sense_id": "7b8f4fba-d4cc-3c1b-bf33-86afd2a1ad8c",
                                                "text": "Max lui tendit le Polaroïd d’une tête tranchée qu’il déposa au milieu de la table."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1668af4-5d88-4e9f-832f-a2f1f0e5fbdb",
                                                "sense_id": "7b8f4fba-d4cc-3c1b-bf33-86afd2a1ad8c",
                                                "text": "Elle en extirpa un appareil photo, l’ajusta et appuya vite sur le déclencheur. Le Polaroïd sortit aussitôt."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
